From bcf374929499e763b1aa83459b0d491e95972c03 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: homelab <homelab@emrys.dev>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 02:56:29 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/7] core: own every snapshot with a user-<name> tag

Snapshot gets no new column: ownership is a user-<username> tag written once,
when the row is created, and preserved by every later tag edit. Snapshot.save()
already routes creation through save_tags(), so that is the one choke point.

The Tag default manager now hides user-* names, which is what makes them
invisible in every tag index, picker, autocomplete, card and API response at
once instead of template by template. Tag.all_objects is the unfiltered
manager for the ownership records themselves.

An add with no resolvable owner is left untagged and therefore invisible;
core/user_scope.py documents the resolution order and the reasoning.
---
